# Draft knowledge entry: Boost.Python 3.12 CMake discovery on HarmonyOS PC
id: DRAFT-boost-python312-cmake-discovery
trigger_tool: cmake|conan|findpython
phase: configure|build|consumer-link
error_signature: "Boost.Python|BOOST_ENABLE_PYTHON|Could NOT find Python|Python.h not found|libboost_python312|Boost::python312|undefined reference to Py_"

severity: 2
category: boost|python|cmake|conan|ohos
match_keywords: Boost.Python, Python 3.12, FindPython, Python_EXECUTABLE, Python_LIBRARY, Python_INCLUDE_DIR, libboost_python312, eigenpy

title: Boost.Python packages should pin FindPython to the OHOS CPython ABI used by consumers
root_cause: >
  Boost's CMake release can find the build host Python or an unversioned target Python when
  cross-building. Boost.Python embeds the selected CPython ABI into the library name and link
  interface, so a package built with the wrong interpreter will not provide the Boost::python312
  target or libboost_python312.so required by Python 3.12 consumers such as eigenpy.
affected_scope: >
  Boost 1.90 CMake-based Conan recipes and downstream C++/Python binding packages on HarmonyOS
  PC that require Boost.Python for the target CPython runtime.
verification_cmd: |
  # In the recipe, print the selected interpreter, include directory, library, and version.
  conan create archives/b/boost/1.90.0.2.1 -pr:h ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -r=ohpcd --build=missing
  # Then confirm the package exports libboost_python312 and the Boost::python312 component.

rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: pin-findpython-from-target-runtime
rec_description: >
  Discover the OHOS CPython interpreter that downstream packages will use, query its sysconfig
  values, and pass Python_EXECUTABLE, Python_ROOT_DIR, Python_INCLUDE_DIR, Python_LIBRARY, and
  Python_FIND_STRATEGY=LOCATION through CMakeToolchain cache variables. Set BOOST_ENABLE_PYTHON
  and reject a non-3.12 interpreter when the downstream ABI requirement is Python 3.12. In OHOS
  smoke tests, link the absolute Python_LIBRARY rather than inheriting optional system libs from
  Python::Python.
rec_command: |
  tc.variables["BOOST_ENABLE_PYTHON"] = True
  tc.cache_variables["Python_EXECUTABLE"] = python["executable"]
  tc.cache_variables["Python_ROOT_DIR"] = python["prefix"]
  tc.cache_variables["Python_INCLUDE_DIR"] = python["include_dir"]
  tc.cache_variables["Python_LIBRARY"] = python["library"]
  tc.cache_variables["Python_FIND_STRATEGY"] = "LOCATION"
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: conan-cmaketoolchain-findpython-cache

fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: fail-fast-on-abi-mismatch
fallback_description: >
  If the target Python headers or libpython cannot be found, mark the dependency as missing for
  the Python runtime package instead of letting CMake fall back to a host Python. A successful
  package must include the ABI-specific Boost.Python library and a real consumer link test.
fallback_command: |
  rg -n "FindPython|Python_EXECUTABLE|Python_LIBRARY|boost_python" build logs archives/b/boost/1.90.0.2.1
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual-diagnosis

forbid_1_pattern: "Python_EXECUTABLE.*usr/bin/python|host Python|without.*Python_LIBRARY"
forbid_1_reason: A host or incomplete Python selection can produce a package that configures but cannot link target consumers.
forbid_1_consequence: Downstream packages miss Boost::python312 or fail with libpython/Py_* link errors.
forbid_2_pattern: "copy.*libboost_python|symlink.*boost_python|pretend.*Boost::python312"
forbid_2_reason: Boost.Python must be built against the matching CPython ABI; renaming or aliasing another library hides an ABI mismatch.
forbid_2_consequence: The package may pass metadata checks while crashing or failing to resolve Python symbols at runtime.

principles: target-runtime-first, abi-specific-validation, real-consumer-link
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of: eigenpy-3.13.0

